`FileHandle.write()` returns `{ bytesWritten }`. Ignoring this value means short writes (due to signals, disk limits, or special filesystems) are silently ignored, resulting in truncated or corrupted downloaded files. `FileHandle.writeFile(buffer)` guarantees the entire buffer is written or throws an error, which is safer for download chunks.

